actors: Operator | This app | Lab IdP | Archive agent

step: An archive job is in flight, and the operator is watching its trace
msg: Operator -> This app: open the trace
text: One trace id covers the request, the token exchange, the hand-off and every
  call so far, from both services. The tidy agent has already passed the filing
  on, and the archive agent is part way through it.

step: The operator hits the switch for the first agent
msg: Operator -> This app: cut off tidy-agent
note: This app: may_decide? admin or sponsor
text: Only an admin or that agent's sponsor may do this. The request carries the
  trace id the operator is looking at, so the cut-off lands in the same story.

step: The app asks the IdP to stop honouring it
msg: This app -> Lab IdP: cut off, by whom
note: Lab IdP: client marked cut off
text: The IdP records the client as cut off, with who did it and why. From now on
  it issues that agent no token and accepts it as no one's delegate.

step: The app ends what the agent left waiting
note: This app: approvals, tasks, hand-offs
text: Pending approvals, claimed tasks and unfinished hand-offs belonging to the
  agent are ended and their tokens wiped, so nobody can approve a request from
  an agent that no longer exists.

step: The archive agent makes its next call
msg: Archive agent -> This app: read notes
text: Its token was made for it, not for the tidy agent, but it came through the
  tidy agent. The API asks the IdP whether it is active, as it does on every call.

step: The IdP looks at the whole history of the token
msg: This app -> Lab IdP: POST /introspect
note: Lab IdP: via tidy-agent, cut off
text: The check is made fresh, and it covers the client the token was issued to,
  the agent acting, and every agent in `via`. One of them is cut off.

step: The next action is refused, and the trace shows who stopped it
msg: This app -> Archive agent: 401 not active
note: This app: audit: refused
text: One request cycle after the switch, the chain stops. The same timeline now
  has the operator's cut-off, the IdP's record of it, and the refusal.
